title: "Finch song's power-law signal is reproduced by finite memory alone"
abstract: "In pre-registered tests, the exponential-plus-power-law decay read as a sign of hierarchy in birdsong appeared in all 100 finch songs generated from each bird's own short-memory syntax, and in 92 to 100% of simulated finite-state worlds with pooled birds or bouts. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
